ok","book","book","book","book","book","best","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","good","mistake","excellent","best","best","best","good","good","excellent","best","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","inaccuracy","best","best","best","good","best","good","miss","best","excellent","best","great","best","best","best","good","best","inaccuracy","great","best","best","excellent","best","best","brilliant","great","best","good","best","best","best","good","best","best","best","inaccuracy","best","best","good","inaccuracy","inaccuracy","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","great","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","great","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","excellent","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","excellent","excellent","excellent","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","inaccuracy","inaccuracy","best","best","excellent","excellent","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","good","good","best"],"moments":[{"ply":36,"name":"18…Bg7","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"18…Bg7 is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 50% to 40%.","points":["White answers 19.f5, which takes e6 away from the Black queen on d7.","Better was 18…gxf4 (0.00), which takes the pawn on f4."],"better":"18…gxf4 trades pawns and leaves White with an isolated pawn on g2. After 19.gxf4 c5 20.Bb5 Qf5 21.Be2 Qxc2+ 22.Kxc2 Rg8 23.dxc5 Bxc5 24.g3, the queens come off (0.00)."},{"ply":57,"name":"29.Rf3","cls":"miss","color":"w","headline":"29.Rf3 lets the win slip: 29.Rc1 kept White winning. White's winning chances go from 76% to 62%.","points":["Black answers 29…Bxb5, which takes the bishop on b5.","Better was 29.Rc1 (+3.12): the rook takes the half-open c-file, aiming at the c5 pawn."],"better":"29.Rc1 takes the half-open c-file, aiming at the c5 pawn. Engine line: 29…Bf8 30.Nc6+ Bxc6 31.Bxc6 Qc7 32.Qb3+ (+3.12)."},{"ply":61,"name":"31.Qxd7","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"31.Qxd7! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the queen on d7.","The next best move, 31.Qc2, would drop White's winning chances from 62% to 47% (−0.37).","31.Qxd7 wins a pawn and trades off the attacked queen instead of losing it to …Qxa4.","Takes the queen on d7 and wins a pawn once the captures settle.","Black was threatening …Qxa4, winning the queen. The queen takes something with it instead.","Black answers 31…Rxd7, taking back."]},{"ply":68,"name":"34…Rc7","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"34…Rc7! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The rook takes the open c-file, aiming at the knight on c5.","Attacks the knight on c5, which is undefended.","The next best move, 34…Re7, would drop Black's winning chances from 48% to 25% (+2.97).","34…Rc7 gets the rook out of the way of Nxd7+ and threatens …e4, winning a rook, picking it up with 36…Bxc3.","White was threatening Nxd7+, winning a rook and a rook. The rook steps away.","It threatens …e4, winning a rook, picking it up with 36…Bxc3, so White has to spend the next move on it."]},{"ply":74,"name":"37…f2","cls":"brilliant","color":"b","headline":"37…f2!! A real sacrifice: Black gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Leaves the rook on c7 where it can be taken.","Taking is too dangerous: White's best reply is 38.Rh1 Rd7 39.Nb4 a5 instead (the engine rates it +0.06).","Creates a passed pawn on f2: no enemy pawn can stop it any more.","Moves the attacked pawn to safety.","37…f2 threatens …f1=Q+, with mate in 4, and stops gxf3.","It threatens …f1=Q+, with mate in 4, so White has to spend the next move on it."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"37…f2!! leaves the rook on c7 hanging. Taking it lets Black's pawn become a queen."},{"title":"What Black gives up","text":"The rook on c7 is attacked by the knight on d5, and 37…f2 doesn't save it. That's a whole rook on offer."},{"title":"What it does instead","text":"It threatens …f1=Q+ and mate."},{"title":"If White takes the rook","text":"38.Nxc7 is met by 38…f1=Q+. Then 39…Qe2 threatens mate, and 40…Qxa6 takes the knight on a6. Black ends up 6 points of material ahead: Black is winning (−5.55)."},{"title":"White's best try","text":"White's best is to leave the rook alone and play 38.Rh1. Black answers 38…Rd7, and the rook on c7 gets away, threatening …Rxd5, winning a knight. Then 39…a5 threatens …axb4, winning a knight, and 41…Rb7 adds pressure on the b2 pawn. Material is level and Black holds the balance (+0.06)."}]},{"ply":75,"name":"38.Rh1","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"38.Rh1! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The next best move, 38.Ne3, would drop White's winning chances from 51% to 5% (−7.93).","38.Rh1 stops the mate threat …f1=Q+.","Black was threatening …f1=Q+, with mate in 4. Rh1 takes care of it.","The engine's plan continues with Nb4 and Nc2: this move is the first step.","Black answers 38…Rd7, attacking the knight on d5, which is undefended.","Engine line: 38…Rd7 39.Nb4 a5 40.Nc2 Bf6 41.Rf1 (+0.02)."]},{"ply":109,"name":"55.Rb4","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"55.Rb4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Shores up the b2 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (2 against 1).","The next best move, 55.Rxd4+, would drop White's winning chances from 50% to 14% (−5.04).","55.Rb4 stops …Rxb2+.","Black was threatening …Rxb2+, winning a pawn. Rb4 takes care of it.","Black answers 55…Rg2, attacking the g5 pawn, which is undefended.","Engine line: 55…Rg2 56.Rb3+ Kc4 57.Rb4+ Kc5 58.Rb8 (0.00)."]},{"ply":129,"name":"65.Rb4","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"65.Rb4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked rook to safety.","Shores up the b2 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (2 against 1).","The next best move, 65.Rc1, would drop White's winning chances from 50% to 0% (#−12).","65.Rb4 stops the mate threat …Rxb2+.","Black was threatening …Rxb2+, with mate in 5. Rb4 takes care of it.","Black answers 65…Kc2, leaving White with a king with pawns missing from its shelter."]}],"opening":{"name":"Queen's Gambit Declined: Ragozin Defense","eco":"D38","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 11…Nd7: 22 moves in all, 11 by White and 11 by Black.","Theory runs out after 11…Nd7: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}